                    {
                        "sense_id": "abd78054-59ed-3217-ac66-3bb4d6eecfad",
                        "entry_id": "eb7d8e33-2834-34c3-83c5-f7cb981bf6dc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An evil or otherwise sinister counterpart of another person or thing."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8c11c511-a11c-4700-a515-7aa0b2480be1",
                                "sense_id": "abd78054-59ed-3217-ac66-3bb4d6eecfad",
                                "text": "Is there an academic way to say that one thing is the Wario of another thing? Like, the demonic version of that thing, but the two are inseparably linked?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a17aff17-d8c7-4b83-83e2-072c0a557478",
                                "sense_id": "abd78054-59ed-3217-ac66-3bb4d6eecfad",
                                "text": "His Wario, meanwhile, began spreading the rumour that the vaccine itself was dangerous, and that the virus that caused polio didn't really exist."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0783121f-05c0-40f9-9e02-9033ae03d26b",
                                "sense_id": "abd78054-59ed-3217-ac66-3bb4d6eecfad",
                                "text": "Anthropology is the Wario of sociology."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
